The procedures of the builtin interfaces Word8, Word16, Word32 and
Word64 (this fork; see
LLVM-IR-backend-docs/fixed-width-integer-types-plan.md), through a
generic module instantiated with each of them.  For each width the
same results are printed three times: from inline calls, from
constants the compiler folds, and from procedure values, which call
m3core's WordN modules.  Every line of output should be the same
with every backend and at every optimization level.
